{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>A fire-offering, a sweet savor to YHWH.</b> And it is written, ״ועשיתם שעיר עזים אחד לחטאת״ — and you shall make one he-goat for a sin-offering. You should rouse your understanding to ask how it is that here, on the fiftieth day, it mentions an fire-offering and a he-goat for a sin-offering, seeing that the offering is for the Shekhinah; whereas at the end of the portion of Pinchas, in the section ״וביום הבכורים בהקריבכם מנחה חדשה לה׳״ — you will not find there either fire-offering or sin-offering, because that offering is for the great Name. The Torah intends to hint to you thereby at what befell us on the day of the giving of the Torah, when we saw His glory and His greatness; and corresponding to them, in the Tabernacle we find (Exodus 40:34) ״וכבוד ה׳ מלא את המשכן״ — twice; and likewise in the Temple, which is called (Isaiah 64:10) ״בית קדשנו ותפארתנו״. And this is clear: that this festival of Atzeret alludes to tiferet and to glory, for concerning it is written (Exodus 23:17) ״יראה כל זכורך״, and on it He showed us His great fire and His words we heard from amidst the fire; but in the Atzeret of Shemini you will not find ״יראה כל זכורך״, for it alludes to glory alone. And understand this."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:51.544361551Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}